2 CONT
2 CONT NIIHOLM, Aser, B.A.Sc, P.Eng - It is with great sadness that the family of Aser Niiholm announces his sudden passing, at home in Toronto, at the age of 66, on February 12, 2009. Aser was born on August 13, 1942 in Viinistu, Harjum
2 CONC aa, Estonia, the cherished son of Elmerise and Leo Niiholm (both deceased). He was the beloved brother of Maie Ilves and her husband Dr. Riivo Ilves of Albany, New York, and adored uncle of Katriina Larissa Ilves of New York City 
2 CONC and Eerik Riivo Ilves and his wife Katie McCallum of Victoria, British Columbia. He will also be greatly missed by relatives in Estonia and many relatives and friends in Toronto. After fleeing Estonia in 1943, Aser and his parents
2 CONC  spent eleven months in Finland and seven years in Sweden, where they were joined by sister Maie. The Niiholm family immigrated to Canada in July 1951, settling in Toronto. Aser graduated from the University of Toronto as an elect
2 CONC rical engineer in 1966 and started to work at Square D Canada (now Schneider Electric), where he stayed for the next 43 years. Aser's life was defined by his caring for others, from his professional customers and colleagues, to hi
2 CONC s family and all others around him. He assisted both parents through to the end of their lives and continued to be a primary support for multiple family friends, fittingly, up until his very last evening. His enduring legacy to th
2 CONC ose who knew him will be one of expertise, caring, and kindness. We will miss his offbeat sense of humour and never-ending supply of jokes, but most of all we will miss his big heart. 
